            <ArticleTitle>Celiac disease presenting as entero-enteral intussusception.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cramping abdominal pain with intermittent intestinal obstruction finally prompted investigation in a 4 1/2-year-old boy with severe failure to thrive (FTT). An entero-enteric intussusception was corrected, and celiac disease was identified as the cause of his inanition. Concomitant FTT and cramping abdominal pain should prompt investigation for celiac disease and small-bowel intussusception.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
